{"absent_by_family": {"adb": 24, "apktool": 2, "application": 15, "artifact": 19, "browser": 9, "direct": 30, "electron": 5, "enhanced": 13, "firmware": 2, "flutter": 2, "frida": 9, "javascript-runtime": 2, "jeb": 4, "managed": 7, "native": 26, "pcap": 2, "session": 17}, "doc_excerpt": {"docs/rea-native/APK_SIGNATURE_NATIVE.md": [{"line": 20, "text": "\nNo result establishes Android installability, trusted signer identity, validity dates, issuer signatures, chain trust, revocation, app manifest semantics or code safety. The response states these limits at both the verification and signer levels. Android evaluates scheme/SDK selection and signature algorithm preference differently: this tool checks **every declared supported record**, so its record verdict is deliberately not an Android platform verdict.\n\n## Implemented checks\n"}, {"line": 34, "text": "\nv1/JAR signature markers are detected but JAR signatures and per-entry coverage are unverified. v3.1 (`0x1b93ad61`), v3.2 (`0x70e1c89f`), proof-of-rotation, source stamps and external v4 `.idsig` remain explicitly unverified. Unknown block IDs are retained as ID/length/hash observations. DSA, ECDSA SHA-512, verity digests and unknown signature algorithms are unsupported and cannot yield a fully verified native record set. A v3.1/v3.2 block without an examined rotation attribute is reported as newer-scheme lineage not examined, rather than lineage absent.\n\n## Admission and isolation\n"}, {"line": 40, "text": "\nCapture cancellation and its thirty-second checks are cooperative between regular-file reads. They do not interrupt a blocked filesystem read or establish a hard end-to-end capture deadline. The current MCP path forwards cancellation through the handler token and does not abort the handler on ordinary cancellation or transport EOF. Direct Rust callers that abort or drop this public async future during file I/O are outside the qualified lifecycle contract: an already running Tokio blocking read can outlive the caller and its outer permit. The six public-MCP lifecycle gates cover the worker stage after capture, not stalled-filesystem reads or runtime shutdown during stalled I/O.\n\nProduction parsing runs in the stdin-only `rea-apk-signature-worker` with no source path, runtime credentials or inherited environment. The worker sets resource limits and, on Linux, parent-death binding and the existing post-read seccomp policy. The controller enforces cancellation and an independent wall deadline, then explicitly kills and reaps the child on failure. No APK is installed, executed, extracted, fetched or modified.\n"}], "docs/rea-native/SOURCE_MAP.md": [{"line": 104, "text": "output refusal and the wall-clock deadline kill and reap the owned child before\nthe operation relinquishes ownership. Under the current cooperative MCP\ncancellation lifecycle, the input-read permit stays held until that read has\nactually completed. Arbitrary abort or drop by a direct Rust caller is outside\nthis qualified path: an already started blocking filesystem operation can"}], "docs/rea-native/compatibility/README.md": [{"line": 16, "text": "\nThe success result deliberately says `mapping_check: PASS` and `raw_reference_authenticity: NOT_REVERIFIED`. It establishes repository consistency with a previously authenticated snapshot; it does **not** read or reauthenticate the original schemas, npm tarball, upstream source bytes or behavioral oracle. The normal CI gate does not depend on the expiring Actions artifact described below. Runtime commit metadata records the sampling baseline only; the gate binds file contents and never requires the current Git HEAD to equal an embedded commit SHA.\n\n## Reproduce full input authentication\n"}, {"line": 56, "text": "\nDesktop has an explicitly observed Ghidra 12.2 launcher, JDK 25 executable and JADX directory outside the process PATH. Chrome/Chromium, GDB/binutils and a pocket4 Apktool installation were also discovered. A discovered path is not a license, compatibility or lifecycle test. JEB/Frida/TShark/Binwalk/Unblob and other selected engines were not found in the bounded PATH/directory observations; that is not a claim that they are absent everywhere. JEB license state remains NOT_PROBED.\n\nFirmware and PCAP corpus work is actionable code/testing work: the pinned upstream includes a Python tar/gzip + host-compiler firmware generator with an independent byte/offset oracle and an owned offline Ethernet/IPv4/TCP capture generator. Provider stubs are explicitly identified and cannot qualify an engine. The observation file links these exact sources rather than inventing a missing-corpus blocker.\n"}, {"line": 58, "text": "\nFirmware and PCAP corpus work is actionable code/testing work: the pinned upstream includes a Python tar/gzip + host-compiler firmware generator with an independent byte/offset oracle and an owned offline Ethernet/IPv4/TCP capture generator. Provider stubs are explicitly identified and cannot qualify an engine. The observation file links these exact sources rather than inventing a missing-corpus blocker.\n\n## Historical 1d9ea7e native release observations\n"}, {"line": 124, "text": "\nThe current finite external observations bind one 18,437,864-byte release,\nSHA-256 `aa580409a73bc2e0927ead93d32634239051a39fc951c3c2a92d5a1dece8347a`,\nbuilt with production/test/script source frozen at\n`ed74d9dbf04b97fad38112c2ac08127bf99b3590`."}, {"line": 125, "text": "The current finite external observations bind one 18,437,864-byte release,\nSHA-256 `aa580409a73bc2e0927ead93d32634239051a39fc951c3c2a92d5a1dece8347a`,\nbuilt with production/test/script source frozen at\n`ed74d9dbf04b97fad38112c2ac08127bf99b3590`.\nThe release runner, Source Map runner and corrected full Rust matrix record"}, {"line": 134, "text": "\n| Current finite observation | Receipt and limits |\n| --- | --- |\n| Release build and Source Map | [Corrected release archive](../../qualification/rea-final-source-map-release-20261104-r3/README.md): build passed; actual REA 8 fixtures/217 queries; 7 direct consumer agreements plus one preserved nested-offset divergence with an independent equivalent golden; 7 public MCP gates. |\n| ASAR and selected JavaScript | [Corrected archive](../../qualification/rea-asar-javascript-final-release-20261104-r3/README.md): 7/7 original planned commands; real ASAR producer/range verification, ASAR cancellation and deadline; normal JS/Babel/manual golden and JS cancellation. This plan contains no separately exercised JS deadline branch. |"}, {"line": 166, "text": "The earlier 18,437,832-byte release,\nSHA-256 `0595fbf02e0f492bd151fec97eb90cb704a88810e9415b90582d348f3db99b6a`,\nwas built from `b857dc7d646dc938e29a51fa82a5856d9b96f842`, with selected\n641-file digest `0ab735bb69893f88ea4f81c73d5d64d5220d234d3ead90cba88c55542eec9abb`.\nIts [Source Map](../../qualification/rea-final-source-map-release-20261104-r2/README.md),"}, {"line": 184, "text": "\nThe recovered artifact includes 418 finite-number cases, corpus digest `9507bba36f7de741ad9a0100516cdaf0a85b496d11feb34e0b4fd8afe1d755fc`, and the original npm ELF-note Evidence record. These were replayed in native Rust at baseline `310add6db47bcfbed3545432eb528a72f5eb6dcd` using the existing ignored tests. Each filter actually executed one test; both passed. The test loops over the authenticated 418-case input. This exercises the Evidence semantic commitment and selected identity invariants, not all 229 operations.\n\n```sh\nREA_REAL_FLOAT_EVIDENCE_JSON=/absolute/rea-reference-cache/oracle/REA_6_8_0_FINITE_NUMBER_EVIDENCE.json cargo test --locked --lib -j4 real_npm_fractional_reference_evidence_matches_native -- --ignored --test-threads=1"}]}, "files": {"docs/rea-native/APK_SIGNATURE_NATIVE.md": {"bytes": 14192, "sha256": "4028b4f301c6e47cd5e48a0969617ed246eac5ec30de16e30cb0775dd601d281"}, "docs/rea-native/ASAR.md": {"bytes": 12011, "sha256": "7c48c588bc75ea925e9a1475b4890bddddf1aa3c60ca681a98633df7d0d0a1f6"}, "docs/rea-native/SOURCE_MAP.md": {"bytes": 8908, "sha256": "7e8e854eb33d744b0b638134382356c5becaf7092586347abbcc2f67abe85c16"}, "docs/rea-native/compatibility/README.md": {"bytes": 23372, "sha256": "7af78ddb206734f3867c3db02646666d48fd46f0120cc9c089f2357770be5d20"}, "docs/rea-native/compatibility/REA_6_8_0_CAPABILITY_MAP.json": {"bytes": 95309, "sha256": "99e07b5ab23877f8b2665de27bbdd83c5e9fe813e9e303be93e8522813de15d3"}, "docs/rea-native/compatibility/REA_6_8_0_LEDGER.json": {"bytes": 738822, "sha256": "a571d19af36edea73bd0585291eee85649dc4728741cbc7fd67f8ac6cba2b9f9"}}, "head": "2623fad7a42e66ead9b4bc254a99d06a900e331b", "native_interfaces": ["rea_compare_web_captures", "rea_inspect_apk_signature", "rea_inspect_application", "rea_inspect_archive", "rea_inspect_artifact", "rea_inspect_asar", "rea_inspect_javascript_graph", "rea_inspect_javascript_package", "rea_inspect_model", "rea_inspect_source_map", "rea_inspect_web_capture", "rea_model_session_list", "rea_model_session_open", "rea_model_session_query", "rea_model_session_read", "rea_read_asar_member", "rea_read_model", "rea_read_preview", "rea_replay_web_entry", "rea_retain_preview", "rea_static_cancel", "rea_static_profiles", "rea_static_read", "rea_static_start", "rea_static_status", "rea_verify_evidence"], "partial": [{"family": "artifact", "name": "inspect_model_artifact", "remaining_behavior": "Upstream Evidence, exact supported type/layout/metadata semantics and default limits, all error/detail/view cases", "required_gates": ["contracts", "results", "evidence", "typed_outcomes", "limits_and_cancellation", "source_package_boundary", "format_architecture_corpus", "retention_and_pagination", "effects_and_recovery"], "routes": ["rea_inspect_model", "rea_read_model", "rea_model_session_open", "rea_model_session_list", "rea_model_session_query", "rea_model_session_read"]}, {"family": "artifact", "name": "inspect_gpu_code_objects", "remaining_behavior": "Complete ELF/PE/fatbin/CUBIN/PTX/HIP/CCOB layout and kernels plus exact u